  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_jit_trace",
    "file": "php-src/ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_trace.c",
    "description": "The tracing JIT incorrectly preserves/propagates stack state and refcount ownership across the two-opcode ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM/OP_DATA sequence when an operand is an indirect global and evaluation can invoke user code. A warning invokes the registered Closure, which reassigns the aliased global, but the trace still treats the pre-callback temporary/indirect value as valid. On side exit, the VM therefore destructs a stale temporary in ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM_SPEC_VAR_UNUSED_OP_DATA_TMP_HANDLER (zend_vm_execute.h:27567); destroying that temporary array releases the Closure object even though EG(user_error_handler) still contains it. Request shutdown subsequently dereferences that freed Closure in zend_shutdown_executor_values. The VM destructor and shutdown code are only the free/crash sites; the missing callback/alias invalidation is in trace construction/state tracking.",
    "conditions": "Run under tracing JIT and make the expression hot enough to execute as a trace. Register a Closure with set_error_handler(), then execute a ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM whose op1 is a VAR/temporary and whose nested dimension evaluation uses an indirect global (as in set_error_handler(function(){ $GLOBALS['a']=''; })[] = $a[$\\xff] = ''). The undefined variable/dimension lookup must emit a warning, invoking the Closure; the callback must reassign the same global while the outer assignment is in progress. A subsequent trace side exit/VM continuation frees the stale temporary, leaving EG(user_error_handler) dangling, and normal request shutdown triggers the reported heap-use-after-free."
  },
